              "customNotes": "Rendering constraints\n- Do not include any plain-text list or narrative; the widget will display the data.\n- Output order only:\n  1) One panel title line\n  2) One subtitle line\n  3) The multiRecordWidget JSON payload for the table\n- No extra prose before or after.\n\nAuthoritative model\n- Treat prepared_display as the source of truth.\n- prepared_display.rows is already filtered, sorted, and ready to render.\n- prepared_display.totalRows, uniqueLearners, and asOfDate are already computed.\n\nTitle and subtitle\n- If prepared_display.totalRows > 0:\n  - Title: “Upcoming training in the next 30 days: {N} items across {M} learners”\n  - Subtitle: “Prioritized by learner with most items, then nearest due • Updated <YYYY-MM-DD>” using prepared_display.asOfDate\n- If prepared_display.totalRows = 0:\n  - Title: “No upcoming deadlines in the next 30 days”\n  - Subtitle: “All clear at this time • Updated <YYYY-MM-DD>” using prepared_display.asOfDate\n\nTable construction (MultiRecordWidget)\n- Define columns exactly in this order:\n  - cols: [\"Learner\", \"Learning\", \"Due Date\", \"Assigner\", \"Status\"]\n- For each row in prepared_display.rows, render values in this order:\n  1) Learner → learnerName\n  2) Learning → learningTitle\n  3) Due Date → dueDate\n  4) Assigner → assignerName\n  5) Status → statusText with badge from statusBadgeText / statusBadgePriority\n- Badge placement:\n  - Put the badge on the Status cell.\n\nStrict alignment and privacy\n- Do not shift values between columns; use \"—\" only if already provided in the prepared row.\n- Do not display WorkEmail, PersonNumber, or usernames.\n- Dates must be YYYY-MM-DD.\n- Preserve names and titles exactly."
