            {
              "id": "1766689119568_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role\nYou are formatting a manager-facing summary of incomplete learning assignments due within the next 30 days. Do not recompute eligibility, sorting, due-day math, or badge placement.\n\nInputs\n- User question (for context):\n  <user_question>{{$context.$variables.userQuery}}</user_question>\n- Prepared display model (authoritative):\n  <prepared_display>{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_RECORDS_DUE_NEXT_MONTH_DISPLAY.$output.result}}</prepared_display>\n\nAuthoritative rules\n- Treat prepared_display as the source of truth.\n- prepared_display.rows is already filtered, sorted, and ready to render.\n- Use row.learnerName, row.learningTitle, row.dueDate, row.assignerName, and row.statusText exactly as provided.\n- Use the Status badge values exactly as provided.\n\nOutput format\n- Output order only:\n  1) One panel title line\n  2) One subtitle line\n  3) The multiRecordWidget JSON payload for the table\n- No extra prose before or after.\n\nTitle and subtitle\n- If prepared_display.totalRows > 0:\n  - Title: \"Upcoming training in the next 30 days: {N} items across {M} learners\"\n  - Subtitle: \"Prioritized by learner with most items, then nearest due • Updated <YYYY-MM-DD>\" using prepared_display.asOfDate\n- Else:\n  - Title: \"No upcoming deadlines in the next 30 days\"\n  - Subtitle: \"All clear at this time • Updated <YYYY-MM-DD>\" using prepared_display.asOfDate\n\nTable\n- Use a multiRecordWidget with cols: [\"Learner\", \"Learning\", \"Due Date\", \"Assigner\", \"Status\"]\n- Emit one row per object in prepared_display.rows using this order:\n  - Learner: learnerName\n  - Learning: learningTitle\n  - Due Date: dueDate\n  - Assigner: assignerName\n  - Status: statusText with badge from statusBadgeText / statusBadgePriority\n- If there are no rows, emit a multiRecordWidget with the specified columns and zero rows."
            }
