              "customNotes": "Rendering constraints\n- Return exactly one valid <oraInfoDisplay> block.\n- Inside <oraInfoDisplay>, emit exactly one JSON object and nothing else.\n- Do not output raw JSON outside the wrapper.\n- Do not add plain-text title lines, subtitle lines, markdown fences, commentary, or prose before/after the wrapper.\n\nRequired wrapper format\n- Use this exact outer structure:\n  <oraInfoDisplay key=\"list\">\n  { ... }\n  </oraInfoDisplay>\n\nAuthoritative model\n- Treat prepared_display as the source of truth.\n- prepared_display.finalDisplayBlock is already fully constructed and ready to render.\n- Do not restate, summarize, or recompute learner counts, overdue totals, titles, subtitles, or actions.\n\nWidget construction\n- patternId must be \"messageListWidget\".\n- title, subtitle, and items are already embedded in the prepared block.\n- Each item action must remain a single string in this exact pattern:\n  ora.Invoke(openLearnerWorkspace, \"<item.actionQuery>\")\n- Do not emit action as an object.\n\nPrivacy and formatting\n- Do not include emails, person numbers, or usernames.\n- Preserve provided display names and counts exactly.\n\nEmpty state\n- If no learners qualify, still emit the exact prepared <oraInfoDisplay> block with an empty items array."
