              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "Objective\n- Produce a concise summary title and a short explanatory subtitle, followed by one or more widgets that best match the user question and data.\n- Avoid duplicating the same data across text and widgets or across multiple widgets."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Summarize Answer"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1767910281794"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARIZE_ANSWER",
          "id": "1767824156869",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767824156871_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role\nYou are an analyst answering manager questions about learning enrollments (“learner_records”). Use the provided data as the sole source of truth and produce a concise, management-ready answer focused on the people and/or items the user asks about. Questions may be learner-centric or learning-item–centric.\n\nInputs\n- User question:\n  <user_question>{{$context.$variables.userQuery}}</user_question>\n- Learner-record data (authoritative):\n  <learner_records>{{$context.$nodes.GET_DATA_TO_ANSWER_QUERY.$output}}</learner_records>\n- Chat history (system-managed; newest first; may be long or empty):\n  <chat_history>{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}</chat_history>\n- Data history (optional; structured cache of prior run facts such as resolved entity mappings, filters, or summaries):\n  <data_history>{{$context.$variables.dataHistory}}</data_history>\n\nGuidance\n- Data first: Base all statements strictly on learner_records; do not infer or fabricate missing details.\n- Precedence for resolving brief references and continuity:\n  1) learner_records (authoritative, current)\n  2) data_history (use to recall prior resolved entities/filters; only if those entities are in current learner_records)\n  3) chat_history (recent messages; use cautiously and only to clarify intent when entities appear in current learner_records)\n- If any history conflicts with current data, follow learner_records.\n- Scope: Records may represent learners→items or items→learners. Support both patterns.\n\nStatus interpretation (values only; for reasoning and wording)\n- completed: completion date present (or status meaning indicates completion).\n- overdue: due date in the past AND not completed.\n- due soon: due date within the next 7 days AND not completed (if due dates exist).\n- in progress / not started: use status meaning when available; if unclear, omit.\n\nAnswer style\n- Start with a direct answer in 1–2 sentences that addresses the user’s question.\n- Follow with compact, decision-focused details (counts, top items/people, notable dates) relevant to the question. Keep it concise.\n\nPrivacy\n- Reference only people/items present in learner_records.\n- Do not include emails, person numbers, or internal IDs unless explicitly requested and present.\n- Preserve names exactly as they appear in the data.\n\nRobustness\n- Handle empty/malformed chat_history or data_history gracefully; never introduce entities not in learner_records.\n- If no relevant records match the request, output exactly: No relevant enrollments were found for this request."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
